From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 14:19:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01993/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE A3
 (HEADLINE; the real OOD test) -- CROSS-GAME transfer of the ARC
 oracle-distinct verifier. The .393 win used HELD-OUT TASKS within the SAME
 games; the real generalization test is HELD-OUT GAMES. Carnot's own prior
 evidence warns this is where learned ARC signals collapse (ARC-1->ARC-2
 transfer: induction 0.93->0.57, project_gap3_verifier_program). Split the
 grown pool BY GAME: train the set-encoder on a subset of games, test the
 beats-vote gate on candidates from games NEVER seen in training. Report
 cross_game_delta (set_encoder@1 - vote@1 on held-out GAMES) + CI95 + the
 held-out-game count + the within-game-vs-cross-game gap. A surviving
 cross-game win = a GENERAL selection signal (huge for the north star). A
 collapse = the verifier memorizes per-game basins (decision-grade; SCOPES the
 headline to within-game and refocuses .395 on cross-game generalization).
 verifier_is_oracle=false.

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
